    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just... hard to think about what \"choosing the quiet\" actually looks like. everything feels so messy and loud right now. when people talk about having dignity at the end, they usually mean not being dragged through the rubble. do you think there's a distinction between just dying when the time comes and actually being the one to decide when the end happens? like, is there any dignity in taking control of it yourself?",
